    "scope": "SKY130 fill, failed attempts, final physical/native circuit checks, partial rule applicability and diode comparison. Not chunk 6 acceptance."
  },
  "resolved": [
    "All final candidates pass the unchanged conservative eight-layer density screen on their original dies; native Magic measurements agree.",
    "All original non-supply capacitance pairs, node resistance values and native device records are exact; new devices are supply-only decaps with individually explained native feedback.",
    "The empty diode_2 CDL master is supplemented from a pinned independent library whose every polygon layer matches the installed cell. Five native diode faults are rejected, including explicit area and perimeter controls.",
    "Windows and Linux independently reconstruct/read back the final geometry, native circuit and diode records with identical data hashes."
  ],
  "retained_failures": [
    "Earlier dense counter fill changed circuit capacitance and is rejected for an unchanged-model handoff.",
    "Intermediate clearance recipes failed density screening; final candidates are counter/UART v20 and APB v22.",
    "Initial remote audit overapplied drawn-mask invariance to nonconducting body-pin annotations; the corrected audit records those annotation changes and still requires every actual mask unchanged within circuit clearance.",
    "Initial diode extraction omitted explicit area comparison and incorrectly accepted an area fault. The corrected deck enables both dimensions and rejects all five faults."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Reconcile every required periphery/error-catalog rule with executable semantics and controls; 329 periphery rows still require execution review.",
    "Resolve the published x.20 IP_block pin-spacing row with missing numeric value and unit; do not invent an acceptance threshold.",
    "Complete implant enclosure/butting-edge coverage and remaining density/window/oxide applicability for the selected block profile.",
    "Complete final netlist equivalence, bound extracted timing, application integration and delivered Windows/Linux execution for the final fill recipe."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Native engines ran on Linux. Windows reconstruction/report audit is not fresh Windows native execution.",
    "Exact nominal native invariance assumes ideal supplies; it is not distributed RC timing, power-integrity or independent field calibration.",
    "Density screening is not complete foundry density qualification. Complete-chip context and device-family qualification remain later chunks."
  ]
